import std

| The ENEMY brain: a deterministic raider for the seed's NPC Invader
| user (uid "2"). This submodule generates its own module
| (generated/invader.ts) with its own hands (shell/invader.ts), bundled
| separately and injected by the flake's seed step as uid 2's
| users.code — the enemy is world content, but its decision logic is
| spec, checked by the same church as the colony brain. Stage 2 of the
| invader trajectory (docs/evolution-plan.md) repackages the SAME
| bundle as a mods.json bot AI under server/mods/.
|
| The vocabulary is deliberately dumb: the itest needs reproducible
| aggression, not a good player. No randomness, no memory beyond the
| FSM state.

union InvaderState
  slaughtering
  razing
  marching
  loitering

| InvaderEvent is a product of three orthogonal facts, same
| construction and template-literal contract as CreepEvent/TowerEvent:
|
|   foe reach    — foe      hostile creep within attackRange
|                  noFoe    none
|   struct reach — Struct   attackable hostile structure within
|                           attackRange (controller excluded — it is
|                           unattackable and would stall the march)
|                  NoStruct none
|   spawn sight  — Spawn    a hostile spawn exists in the room
|                  NoSpawn  none
|
| The shell computes the event as `${foe}${struct}${spawn}` with foe in
| {"foe","noFoe"}, struct in {"Struct","NoStruct"}, spawn in
| {"Spawn","NoSpawn"}; tsc proves the inferred template-literal union
| is exactly this union. attackRange is the ONE range constant serving
| both reach facts and the attack action (same-filter doctrine: the
| observed fact can never contradict the available action).

union InvaderEvent
  foeStructSpawn
  foeStructNoSpawn
  foeNoStructSpawn
  foeNoStructNoSpawn
  noFoeStructSpawn
  noFoeStructNoSpawn
  noFoeNoStructSpawn
  noFoeNoStructNoSpawn

| The fixed action/target vocabularies the invader hands execute.
|   attack — creep.attack at the resolved target
|   march  — creep.moveTo the resolved target
|   idle   — no API call
|   foeInReach   — lowest-id hostile creep within attackRange
|   structInReach— lowest-id attackable hostile structure within
|                  attackRange (controller excluded)
|   hostileSpawn — closest hostile spawn
|   none         — no target (pairs with idle)
| Lowest-id tie-breaks keep target choice deterministic under equal
| range — reproducibility is the point of this brain.

union InvaderAction
  attack
  march
  idle

union InvaderTargetKind
  foeInReach
  structInReach
  hostileSpawn
  none

type InvaderBehavior
  action: InvaderAction
  target: InvaderTargetKind

| InvaderStateBehaviors is a RECORD with one field per InvaderState
| variant — the same tsc-totality trick as StateBehaviors: the hands
| index invaderBehaviors[state]; a state without a behavior fails the
| build. FIELD ORDER CONTRACT (tower precedent): the FIRST field is the
| machine's initial state — the hands derive the recovery state from
| Object.keys(invaderBehaviors)[0], never from a state literal.

type InvaderStateBehaviors
  marching: InvaderBehavior
  slaughtering: InvaderBehavior
  razing: InvaderBehavior
  loitering: InvaderBehavior

slaughteringBehavior: InvaderBehavior
  InvaderBehavior:
    action: InvaderAction.attack
    target: InvaderTargetKind.foeInReach

razingBehavior: InvaderBehavior
  InvaderBehavior:
    action: InvaderAction.attack
    target: InvaderTargetKind.structInReach

marchingBehavior: InvaderBehavior
  InvaderBehavior:
    action: InvaderAction.march
    target: InvaderTargetKind.hostileSpawn

loiteringBehavior: InvaderBehavior
  InvaderBehavior:
    action: InvaderAction.idle
    target: InvaderTargetKind.none

invaderBehaviors: InvaderStateBehaviors
  InvaderStateBehaviors:
    marching: marchingBehavior
    slaughtering: slaughteringBehavior
    razing: razingBehavior
    loitering: loiteringBehavior

| Context knobs, both consumed mechanically by the hands:
|   attackRange — reach for the foe/struct facts AND the attack action
|                 (melee: 1)
|   repathTicks — moveTo reusePath value; 0 = recompute every tick, so
|                 the march never follows a stale path (determinism
|                 over CPU thrift; the NPC has cycles to burn)

type InvaderContext
  attackRange: Integer
  repathTicks: Integer

invaderAttackRange: Integer
  1

invaderRepathTicks: Integer
  0

invaderContext: InvaderContext
  attackRange: invaderAttackRange
  repathTicks: invaderRepathTicks

| Raider policy: creeps outrank structures outrank the march; nothing
| in reach and no spawn to march on -> loiter. The mapping is
| STATE-INDEPENDENT — all four states carry the IDENTICAL eight
| transitions, so this is a pure policy function
| (InvaderEvent -> InvaderState) in FSM clothing, exactly the tower
| precedent: uniform machine shape, generic interpreter, the state
| still picks the action via invaderBehaviors[state].
|
| Why creeps first: a defender creep blocking the path would otherwise
| let the raider be killed for free while it chews a wall — answer the
| sword before the masonry.

toSlaughteringFoeStructSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.foeStructSpawn
    target: InvaderState.slaughtering
    guard: ()

toSlaughteringFoeStructNoSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.foeStructNoSpawn
    target: InvaderState.slaughtering
    guard: ()

toSlaughteringFoeNoStructSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.foeNoStructSpawn
    target: InvaderState.slaughtering
    guard: ()

toSlaughteringFoeNoStructNoSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.foeNoStructNoSpawn
    target: InvaderState.slaughtering
    guard: ()

toRazingNoFoeStructSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.noFoeStructSpawn
    target: InvaderState.razing
    guard: ()

toRazingNoFoeStructNoSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.noFoeStructNoSpawn
    target: InvaderState.razing
    guard: ()

toMarchingNoFoeNoStructSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.noFoeNoStructSpawn
    target: InvaderState.marching
    guard: ()

toLoiteringNoFoeNoStructNoSpawn: Transition InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Transition:
    event: InvaderEvent.noFoeNoStructNoSpawn
    target: InvaderState.loitering
    guard: ()

slaughteringConfig: StateConfig InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  StateConfig:
    transitions: [toSlaughteringFoeStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeStructNoSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructNoSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructNoSpawn, toMarchingNoFoeNoStructSpawn, toLoiteringNoFoeNoStructNoSpawn]
    label: "Slaughtering"

razingConfig: StateConfig InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  StateConfig:
    transitions: [toSlaughteringFoeStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeStructNoSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructNoSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructNoSpawn, toMarchingNoFoeNoStructSpawn, toLoiteringNoFoeNoStructNoSpawn]
    label: "Razing"

marchingConfig: StateConfig InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  StateConfig:
    transitions: [toSlaughteringFoeStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeStructNoSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructNoSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructNoSpawn, toMarchingNoFoeNoStructSpawn, toLoiteringNoFoeNoStructNoSpawn]
    label: "Marching"

loiteringConfig: StateConfig InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  StateConfig:
    transitions: [toSlaughteringFoeStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeStructNoSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructSpawn, toSlaughteringFoeNoStructNoSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructSpawn, toRazingNoFoeStructNoSpawn, toMarchingNoFoeNoStructSpawn, toLoiteringNoFoeNoStructNoSpawn]
    label: "Loitering"

| Reachability from marching: foe* -> slaughtering, noFoeStruct* ->
| razing, noFoeNoStructNoSpawn -> loitering — all four states
| reachable, every state covers all eight events, no finals, no
| deadlock. generate verifies exactly this.

invaderMachine: Machine InvaderState InvaderEvent InvaderContext
  Machine:
    name: "invader"
    initial: InvaderState.marching
    context: invaderContext
    finals: {}
    states: {InvaderState.slaughtering: slaughteringConfig, InvaderState.razing: razingConfig, InvaderState.marching: marchingConfig, InvaderState.loitering: loiteringConfig}
